        <!-- Troubleshooting -->
        <section id="troubleshooting" class="docs-section">
          <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>

          <h3>Connection test fails</h3>
          <p>
            Click <strong>Test connection</strong> after entering your credentials.
            Nimbus will tell you which specific step failed — DNS resolution, authentication,
            bucket access, or write permission. The most common causes are a typo
            in the Access Key or Secret, or the bucket not existing yet in the selected
            region.
          </p>

          <h3>Images are showing broken after offload</h3>
          <p>
            Check that <strong>Serve From Storage</strong> is enabled and that your
            CDN domain is correctly set. If you are using Cloudflare R2 with a public
            bucket, make sure you have either enabled the
            <code>r2.dev</code> public URL or are using a custom domain pointing at
            your bucket.
          </p>

          <h3>Bulk job is stuck</h3>
          <p>
            Bulk jobs run on WordPress cron. If your host disables WP-Cron on
            web requests (common on managed WordPress hosts), set up a real cron
            job: <code
              >*/2 * * * * wp cron event run --due-now --path=/path/to/wp</code
            >. If you cannot run cron, trigger the tick manually with
            <code>wp nimbus process-pending</code>.
          </p>

          <h3>Log viewer</h3>
          <p>
            Go to <strong>Nimbus → Logs</strong> to see a structured log of every
            offload, restore, rewrite, and purge operation. Filter by level (info
            / warning / error), source, or keyword. Up to 2,000 entries are stored.
            If you need to share a log for support, use the
            <strong>Copy log</strong> button to get a plain-text snapshot.
          </p>

          <h3>Still stuck?</h3>
          <div class="docs-callout">
            Email <a href="mailto:hello@usenimbus.dev">hello@usenimbus.dev</a> with
            a description of the issue and a copy of your Nimbus log. We typically
            respond within one business day.
          </div>
        </section>
